STEPS = [
    "S8-A: DONE and committed (c6a95ae0 .. 6ddfae42, ledger dfd1a8d5). The lead records dfd1a8d5 as the S8-B base. `git status --short` shows only .plan-work/ before S8B-0. No step of S8-B touches a .proto file, a session-core migration, model-gateway source, the BFF or the SPA; a build session checks that with `git diff --stat` at every step.",
    "S8B-0 (mp-contracts; FIRST, alone, its own commit): EXT_CRASH_PARKABLE, LOOP_CRASH_PARK_ENV, loop_crash_park_enabled; the new crash_park.rs with CrashMark, CrashRefusal and crash_reseal; the two golden fixtures and their test. It builds and passes alone and changes no behaviour (nothing calls it yet). Verify: cargo test -q -p mp-contracts. Commit: feat(mp-contracts): the crash-park contract, the marker payload, its switch and crash_reseal (WS03 S8B-0).",
    "S8B-1 (session-core; after S8B-0; may be BUILT in parallel with S8B-2, they share no file but the compose file, where each adds rows in a different service block: the lead applies both, or S8B-1 goes first):\n- loop_checkpoint.rs: the crash TTL, CrashParkOutcome, crash_park_run, seed_marked_fold and the store-level tests;\n- terminalization.rs: the switch and crash_park_active, worker_cipher, the CASE and $4 in the horizon statement and spare_parked_run's third argument, PARK_HELD_REASON_SQL, the worker branch, the metrics, the amended park_spare guard and the new crash_park_violations;\n- the compose rows (switch and TTL);\n- the DB tests.\nIt is dormant: with SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED off the worker is S8-A's (the byte-identity of heartbeat_managed_run_inner and claim_due_recovery is pinned). It needs no executor change to be tested (its fixtures are marked folds written by seed_marked_fold from the S8B-0 fixture). Re-run the committed --ignored loop_checkpoint, park_recovery_db_tests and S8-A park tests green. Verify: cargo test -q -p session-core --bin session-core (session-core is a binary-only crate: there is no --lib target); the DB tests by the lead against a scratch Postgres with --test-threads=1 (park_recovery_db_tests::isolate pushes every other obligation a day out, so the DB tests must not run in parallel). Commit: feat(session-core): the recovery worker parks an eligible active fold at its deadline instead of ending the run, behind SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED (WS03 S8B-1).",
    "S8B-2 (execution-core, the marker and the visible-call fence; after S8B-0; parallel with S8B-1): park.rs (crash_marking_active, CrashStaticFacts, run_crash_parkable as its OWN conjunct list, crash_ineligible_reason, crash_marked, tool_names_derivable, crash_mark_of, is_visible_call, CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT = FALSE; run_parkable and park_fold untouched); fold.rs (Snapshot's one field, build_fold's marker rule, and the four pure accessors arm_fence, is_fenced, lost_ownership and ownership_unproven, which the CrashGate and the visible-call hold use); agent.rs (CrashGate, the hoisted static_facts local, the one per-run info! line, the five Snapshot literals, the visible-call count in effectful_calls, the visible_hold local and the closure's own hold); the compose row; crash_mark_violations and visible_call_violations; the tests of S8B-2 (every marking test asserts only on resumable boundary folds and forces the CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT override explicitly, so none of them changes in S8B-3). With CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT false the marker is NEVER written by configuration, so an image built here is behaviourally S8-A's. Do NOT deploy an image between S8B-2 and S8B-3. Verify: cargo test -q -p execution-core --lib runtime_loop:: and --test durable_loop_contract (all committed rows green, none edited). Commit: feat(execution-core): crash-park eligibility marker on round-boundary folds of read-only pinned runs and a pre-effect fence for plan and delegation calls, inert until the retire fence lands (WS03 S8B-2).",
    "S8B-3 (execution-core, the fence; after S8B-2): fold.rs (OffReason::SelfClosed, note_self_closed, retire); park.rs (must_stop; try_park: note_self_closed in the NotAccepted arm only, and the ambiguous arm closes only under !folds.is_fenced()); agent.rs (LoopContext.heartbeat_floor and run_rounds' last_beat, the loop-top must_stop check, the async-block exit funnel, retire_fence at its two sites, superseded_status); mp-contracts is unchanged here (the window constants landed in S8B-0); the re-anchoring, in the same commit, of the three committed mutation rows the re-indent moves, in TWO meta-tests (the Site B ParkPoint row and the Site A max_rounds row of the_park_writer_guard_goes_red_when_the_code_it_guards_regresses, and the while row of the_park_resume_guards_go_red_when_the_code_they_guard_regresses), with the new mutate_re_in helper, whitespace-insensitive; CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT = true together with CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT_EXPECTED and retire_violations; the tests of S8B-3. This step is what makes marking safe to configure. Verify: cargo test -q -p execution-core --lib runtime_loop:: and the two contract test files (both meta-tests green, every other committed row unedited); cargo fmt --all -- --check (CI runs it, and the async block re-indents run_rounds). No gateway test is run by the build. Commit: feat(execution-core): a marked loop saves a tombstone before it ends the run or raises an approval and stops when it cannot prove it owns the run (WS03 S8B-3).",
    "S8B-4 (execution-core tests; after S8B-1 AND S8B-3): the cross_service_loop_contract pins; store_proofs() Park entry filled with the S8B-1 and S8B-2 tests (store_proof_violations fails when a named test does not exist, so it lands only now); the two switch_table rows; a re-run of every_guard_goes_red_when_the_code_it_guards_regresses and both park meta-tests with every committed row unchanged SINCE S8B-3. Commit: test(execution-core): contract pins for crash-park, the Park store proof and the switch rows (WS03 S8B-4).",
    "S8B-5 (lead, docs and compose comments): the ledger entry, the flip and kill table comment in compose, MODEL_PLANE_STATUS.md, the build-ledger rows; optionally the run-park.ts comment that calls crash_interrupted reserved (a comment-only change).",
    "DEPLOY ORDER: session-core first (dormant), then execution-core (an image holding S8B-2 and S8B-3). Nothing else changes, so no gateway, BFF or SPA redeploy.",
    "FLIP ORDER (with the S8-A flips (1) the S8-0 expiry switch, (2) park recovery, (3) the gateway and BFF park form already on, and the S8-A park resume live-proven): (5) EXECUTION_LOOP_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED in execution-core, with EXECUTION_LOOP_RESUME_ENABLED, AGENT_CONTINUE_AFTER_APPROVAL_ENABLED, EXECUTION_LOOP_CHECKPOINT_ENABLED and EXECUTION_EFFECT_LEDGER_ENABLED already on (EXECUTION_LOOP_PARKING_ENABLED is NOT required); (6) SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED in session-core. BOTH are owner-gated and so is their ORDER, listed as an open question with both options: (5) then (6) is the proposal (the owner reads the per-run armed info! line before session-core acts; execution-core records no metrics), but (5) is NOT observation-only; (6) then (5) is dormant until (5) and bears (5)'s effects only when crash-park is meant to work. (5)'s visible effects on a MARKED run: a loop that meets a run that ended under it (a cancel, a worker terminalization, a duplicate dispatch) or that the store refuses (Denied) stops without a late answer or receipt; a marked loop that overran its credentials (its last round outlived the 60 s margin, ordinary for a delegation round) ends through recovery instead of an immediate failed receipt; one extra tombstone RPC per run end and a pre_effect save before a plan or delegation round.",
    "KILL ORDER: (6) session-core crash park off (no new crash park; existing ones stay spared until the CRASH TTL, claimable and resumable; the crash TTL is still bound because it is read under park_recovery_active()); (5) executor crash park off (no new marks, no tombstone, no ownership stop; loops already running keep the behaviour they started with); then the S8-A kill order (a) to (e). While a crash park exists NONE of the resume lane may go off first: the executor's resume switches; the GATEWAY's own AGENT_CONTINUE_AFTER_APPROVAL_ENABLED and EXECUTION_LOOP_RESUME_ENABLED (model-gateway reads both, and the committed S7 text rolls the gateway back first: S8-B overrides that order while parks exist); the gateway or BFF park form, an image below S8-7 or S8-8 included; an executor image below S8-A. Otherwise those parks are held for the crash TTL and cannot be resumed.",
    "ROLLBACK OF IMAGES: session-core below S8-B only after (6) is off and the crash parks have drained (wait the crash TTL or cancel the runs): an S8-A session-core spares a crash park for the park TTL (24 h by default) and knows no crash TTL. During a rolling deploy replicas of different images share the worker queue, so whichever replica claims an obligation decides and an S8-A replica can spare a crash park under the park TTL; replicas whose switches or descriptor key differ decide differently too: drain before rolling. execution-core below S8-B: marks stop; existing crash parks stay resumable by the S8-A executor. execution-core below S8-A: never while a crash park exists. A session-core below S8-A is always safe (it cannot crash-park).",
"S8B-6 LIVE PROOF (lead only; NEEDS THE OWNER'S APPROVAL for every docker command, switch flip, TTL change, manual deadline write, MP_TOKEN use, executor kill, paused container and leftover row): stages c0 to c7 as in the tests list; evidence goes to docs/compliance/evidence/live-proof-ws03-s8b-crash-park-<date>.txt. Until it runs, the crash-park paths are recorded as unit- and DB-tested only.",
]

RISKS = [
    "R1 (the central one): nothing calls the resume route today. No UI button exists and the owner's S8-A ledger entry keeps the flip owner-gated for that reason. With crash-park on and no resumer, every crash-parked run ends outcome_unknown at the 15-minute deadline PLUS the crash TTL (about 75 minutes with the default one hour, 16 minutes at the 60 s floor) instead of at ~15 minutes, RunDetail shows it resumable for the TTL, and runs.status stays running meanwhile. The crash TTL bounds the extra; the flip question is the owner's (open_questions).",
    "R2: the covered population is real, not empty: every ChatGPT-subscription Do turn from the SPA in a non-Space thread of an org with no MCP tool (a subscription turn sends tools [], plan_mode maps to the read_only rung, and a pinned run is refused without plan_mode unless the effects switch is on), and every API caller sending a pinned plan_mode run with no client tools, that crashes after a tool round while a round is left. Never marked: a run that sends client tool specs, a run of an org with an MCP tool, every effect-capable run, every unpinned run, every approval continuation, a crash in the FIRST round (no fold exists yet), a crash inside a delegation or plan-proposing round (the visible-call fence removes the marker for those rounds, on purpose), and a run that ever raised an approval. These keep the committed ~15 minute outcome_unknown.",
    "R3: the residual duplicate answer, of a HEALTHY loop. If the tombstone save keeps failing for a transient reason (three attempts) while the loop's last heartbeat is recent, the loop proceeds (fail open, as every fold save is). If the append then succeeds and the receipt fails, or the executor crashes in the gap, the run is left non-terminal with its marked fold stored; a crash park at the next deadline and a user continuing would then give a second answer. It needs three consecutive tombstone failures on the same service that then answers the append, plus a failed receipt or a crash, plus a resume: every step is a service failure, correlated only by a flapping replica. A SUPERSEDED loop does not share this residual: it is stopped by the age rule whatever the transport does. Closing R3 exactly needs a durable fact ordered with the append (the v4 thread watermark: a migration and a claim that takes the thread lock); rejected for v1 with that cost, listed for the owner.",
    "R4: behaviour changes of flip (5) for runs that are marked, none of them observation-only: (a) a marked loop that finds the run ended under it (a user cancel, a worker terminalization, a duplicate dispatch: a Stale or Closed answer) now stops with no late answer and no receipt, where committed code appends the answer after the cancel; (b) with a PLANE_TOKEN_TTL longer than 15 minutes a live loop silent past the deadline loses the late answer committed code would append after the worker ended the run; (c) a marked loop whose bearers expired (Denied) but whose last accepted heartbeat is under 780 s old keeps the committed behaviour (an immediate failed receipt), and one silent past that window stops and ends through recovery; the typical overrun is a delegation or plan round, whose stored fold is unmarked (the visible-call fence), so it is never crash-parked and only its failure is delayed to the 15-minute deadline when it is silent that long; (d) a loop that finishes after being superseded is dropped; (e) cost when session-core is degraded: one extra tombstone RPC per run end (up to about 6.4 s of retries before the committed finalize failure) and a pre_effect save before a plan or delegation round (up to the 10 s gated timeout plus one probe before dispatch). By default a silent loop has no late answer anyway (its 300 s session bearer is dead), so (b) matters only for long-lived bearers. These effects are part of the owner's flip decision, not hidden behind it.",
    "R5: drift between crash and resume. A deploy or config change that alters the system prompt, a tool definition, the research kill switch or the server-resolved view makes check_park_fold close the fold at the first continue (park_not_restorable) and the run ends at the renewed deadline; if nobody continues it is held for the crash TTL. Executors are usually killed BY a deploy, so this is the common case for crash parks of a deploy window; its cost is bounded by the crash TTL, not the park TTL. crash_reseal (session-core) and check_park_fold (execution-core) are two functions in two crates: version skew between images shows up as the same park_not_restorable.",
    "R6: coupled-flip drift the worker cannot see. session-core cannot know that the gateway's park form (MODEL_GATEWAY_LOOP_PARKING_ENABLED and the BFF flag, or an image below S8-7 or S8-8) or the executor's resume switches are off. With SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED on and any of them off, a crash park cannot be resumed and is held for the crash TTL. The flip order and the kill order carry the rule; the TTL bounds the damage.",
    "R7: the re-seal opens and re-seals up to 4 MiB inside a transaction holding the run, obligation and fold locks. Acceptable at crash frequency (the same trade the S8 designs accepted); a run's own saves wait on the runs lock for that moment.",
    "R8: a new executor image with the switch on against an old session-core does extra work for nothing: one tombstone RPC at the end of each marked run, marker keys in folds, a pre_effect save before plan and delegation rounds, and the ownership stop. The stop is a new behaviour for marked loops only: the loser of a duplicate dispatch now stops instead of also answering (an improvement), and a loop whose writer double-committed ambiguous saves would stop instead of answering (vanishingly rare, conservative).",
    "R9: the exactness argument assumes effect_class_of and the rung gate agree. effect_class_of is derived from permission::rung_required_for, the function check_autonomy_rung uses; the test a_read_only_rung_refuses_every_call_the_ledger_classes_as_effectful pins it over the offered tool set. A future tool classed as a read that has an effect would break this, and S6, S7 and S8-A rest on the same classification. plan.propose and subagent.* are Read-classed visible writes and are fenced separately (the pre_effect fence of approach 1(a)); a future tool of that kind needs is_visible_call extended.",
    "R10: an unspecified rung is no gate (check_autonomy_rung returns Ok for it) although autonomy::rank ranks it narrowest. S8-B therefore requires the explicit label read_only and plan_mode, and a fold with an unspecified rung is refused (a table row).",
    "R11: the stale-after-ambiguous probe. A loop whose EARLIER save timed out has one retry at seq+1. After a re-seal that retry can match the park's seq and succeed, so a live loop can take back a crash park (and a resume that has claimed but not fenced loses its fence). Exactly one loop still proceeds, because both are saves at one seq; the park is undone because its owner turned out to be alive. Dropping the probe for marked loops was rejected: an ambiguous but committed save would then stop a healthy loop, which is far more frequent. retire_fence's own retries arm the probe too (a first attempt that hits a dead connection is ambiguous, so the second attempt's Stale answer probes at seq+1).",
    "R12: inherited from S8-A. At the TTL boundary the worker can end a park that a live resume has claimed but not yet fenced (a window of seconds). The crash TTL is shorter, so it is reached more often, never more harmfully: the fence then gets run_ended and nothing is dispatched. Changing SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_TTL_SECONDS while crash parks exist moves their horizon at the next pass.",
    "R13: the visible-call fence costs coverage by design and never takes a call away. A plan-proposing round and a delegation round (the longest rounds) save an unmarked pre_effect fold first, so a crash inside one is terminalized, not parked; the next end-of-round fold is marked again. The fence holds a visible call only when ownership is lost; a transient save failure or a writer that failed for another reason (KeyUnavailable, Unimplemented) dispatches it as committed code does, accepting that a crash then parks the marked boundary before the call and a resume repeats it (a second plan proposal, newest wins; a second delegation record).",
    "R14: the tombstone before an approval means a marked loop that pauses cold leaves a non-resumable fold. That is the intent (a run waiting on an approval did not crash). If that save is not confirmed, the approvals fact in crash_park_run still refuses the run, so a stale marked fold can never be parked after an approval.",
    "R15: the DB tests need a scratch Postgres, and the Docker engine on the developer machine wedges (see the project memory). The wiring is therefore also pinned by source guards and by pure unit tests that need no database; the DB tests are the lead's to run, and the live proof is the owner's.",
    "R16: no timestamp enters the crash-park decision, but WHEN the worker looks is still decided by the heartbeat's Utc::now() + 900 s against the database's now() (committed, unchanged). A session-core clock far from the database's moves that moment, as it moves today's terminalization.",
    "R17: execution-core records no metrics (no recorder is installed): the evidence of the marker, the tombstone and a stop is info! lines (one per run says whether marking is armed and, when not, the first failing fact). The owner's gate between (5) and (6) rests on those lines, so the build must keep them content-free and closed-field.",
    "R18: two new visible behaviours on a rolling deploy: a marked loop on an old session-core meets Unimplemented-free saves it accepts (fine), and mixed session-core replicas decide per obligation (a crash park created by an S8-B replica can be spared under the park TTL by an S8-A one): drain before rolling.",
    "R19a: the SPA. A crash-parked run stays running for the deadline plus the crash TTL and sends no run_parked frame (the executor is dead). On every thread open the SPA's follow of an unresumable run sets the composer to its streaming state (a message typed meanwhile is held, not sent) for up to its fixed 15-minute outcome wait, then settles 'unknown', and the next open does it again while the run is non-terminal. The only way out for the user is Stop, which calls cancelRun: it cancels the run and PURGES the crash park, so SPA users would destroy most crash parks before any resume button exists. The prerequisite the owner may set for session-core's switch is concrete: the gateway/BFF projects resumable and park_reason=crash_interrupted (the BFF strips both today) and the SPA renders an 'interrupted' tail that does not hold the composer and has a dismiss action that does not cancel the run.",
    "R19b: configuration skew between session-core replicas (the store switch, park recovery, the crash switch or the descriptor key differ during a rollout): a marked loop whose writer turns Off (loop_checkpoint_disabled) or Failed for a non-ownership reason (KeyUnavailable) cannot fence its exit, while another replica may crash-park the marked fold it stored earlier. The drain-before-rolling rule covers it; it is not designed away.",
    "R19c: poison-run amplification once an AUTOMATIC resumer exists: a run whose next round kills the executor process (an OOM or an abort) is crash-parked, resumed, re-marked and killed again up to MAX_PARKS_PER_RUN = 5 times, and each kill takes every other in-flight run on that executor with it. An automatic resumer needs backoff and a per-run crash budget below the park cap, or a 'crashed on resume' fact that stops re-sealing; S8-B has neither because it has no resumer.",
    "R19d: the stated total wait of an unresumed crash park (the deadline plus the TTL) can overshoot by up to one deadline period: any heartbeat after the re-seal (from a resume that dies between its heartbeat and its fence, or from a superseded loop whose ambiguous save left its writer Active) pushes the obligation's next pass to now + 900 s.",
    "R19: a new user turn on the same thread while a crash park waits: the resume appends its answer after the newer turn (inherited from S8-A risk 4).",
]

INVARIANTS = [
    "A crash park is created by exactly one function, crash_park_run, inside the worker's transaction that holds the run row, the obligation row and then the fold row, and only for an ACTIVE fold of a persistent run whose content passes crash_reseal, which has no row in session_tool_audit_intents and no row in approvals.",
    "mp_contracts::crash_park::crash_reseal is the only decision of what an eligible fold is and what the parked fold is. session-core calls it; the executor's oracle test calls it and then check_park_fold on the result.",
    "The executor writes the marker (one key, crash_parkable, a CrashMark payload) only on a boundary fold (round None, pending None), only when crash_marking_active() and run_crash_parkable and a round is left and parks < MAX hold. A park fold, a pause fold and a pre_effect fold of an open round never carry it. The S8-A park keys stay exclusive to park_fold. With the switch off or CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT false every fold is byte-identical to S8-A's.",
    "The marker's tool fact is computed from the allowlist the loop really runs under (built after a continuation's snapshot replaced the request's tools: it EQUALS the base names or the base names plus tickets.create), in addition to the request-kind fact, the seed kind and the release fact. An approval continuation (segment or in place), a delegated loop, a client-tool or MCP-tool run, a Space run, a ZDR or waived run, an unpinned run, a run with plan_mode false or any rung but read_only never carries the marker and is terminalized at the committed deadline.",
    "A read-only marked run cannot run an effect at any depth: effect_class_of and check_autonomy_rung share rung_required_for. A round that contains a plan.* or subagent.* call is preceded by a pre_effect fold (unmarked, with an open round) for a marked loop, so, after a SUCCESSFUL fence, a crash inside that round is never parked and a stale loop's call is held; after a failed (fail-open) fence a crash may park the marked boundary before the call and a resume repeats it (R13).",
    "A marked (armed) loop ends the run (finalize: the answer append and the terminal receipt, for ANY outcome including typed failures) or raises an approval only after retire_fence returned Ok, or in one of these cases: its writer is not Active and has not lost ownership and is not unproven (a NotAccepted park the loop itself closed, a store that is off, a writer failed for a non-ownership reason); or the proof is unavailable (a Denied or NotFound answer, an unproven writer, or three transient failures) AND the loop's own last accepted heartbeat was SENT less than the fail-open window ago (900 s minus 120 s), measured on its monotonic clock. A Stale or Closed answer, or a writer that lost ownership, ends the loop with Aborted continue_in_progress at any age; so does an unproven answer at or past the window. A stop happens before finalize or the approval: no append, no receipt, no approval. An unarmed loop is untouched. retire_fence has exactly two call sites.",
    "A tombstone is a fold no resume restores (is_resumable() false) and crash_reseal refuses it (NotResumable).",
    "Of one run's tombstone save and one crash-park re-seal exactly one takes effect, because both take the runs row lock and then the fold row lock. If the tombstone commits first the run is never crash-parked afterwards; if the re-seal commits first the loop never ends the run or raises an approval, except that a loop whose earlier save was ambiguous may take the run back through its one probe, in which case the resume's fence is the stale one: exactly one proceeds.",
    "No clock, no messages row and no thread lock enters the crash-park decision. messages.created_at and run_loop_checkpoints.updated_at are never compared; the park's due time and its TTL are database now() on both sides.",
    "An armed loop stops at its next loop top, before the heartbeat and before any inference, when park::must_stop says so: its writer has lost ownership (Stale or Closed), or it is unproven (Denied or NotFound) and the heartbeat age is at or past the fail-open window. The status it returns is an existing closed token, Aborted, which the gateway never treats as a confirmed rejection, so no stream of a superseded loop terminalizes the run. A writer the executor itself turned off after a NotAccepted park, whose own row it closed (Off(SelfClosed)), has lost nothing and finalizes as committed. A marked loop NEVER closes a row it did not write: after an ambiguous park save it does not close expected+1 (that seq may hold the worker's crash park) and keeps its writer Active, so the funnel settles ownership.",
    "A crash park is kind park, state parked, park_reason crash_interrupted, due at once (park_until = now()), anchored at updated_at, with parks incremented by exactly one, the S8-A park keys set from the marker's payload and the marker removed. The executor never writes crash_interrupted and the save RPC still refuses it (park_reason_reserved).",
    "A crash park is spared until updated_at + SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_TTL_SECONDS, which is itself reached only after the 15-minute deadline (bound whenever park recovery is active, whatever the crash switch says) and then terminalized once through the unchanged outcome_unknown path; a typed park keeps the park TTL. Crash parking writes no terminal state and no receipt.",
    "The worker never takes the threads row, a messages row, an approvals row or a ledger row lock for crash parking. The lock order is runs, obligation, fold.",
    "With SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED off, park recovery off or the store off, the worker, the heartbeat and the claim are byte-identical to S8-A's (a source pin and a DB control).",
    "The resume of a crash park is the S8-A resume, unchanged: the claim by the empty reference, check_park_fold, route_request, the fence at the claimed seq. The resumed loop is itself marked (seed Parked) and shares the park cap of 5 with typed parks.",
    "Cancel, the TTL and any terminal transition purge a crash park exactly as they purge a typed park.",
    "S8-B adds no proto field, no migration, no closed token, and changes no model-gateway, BFF or SPA source. run_parkable, StaticFacts and park_fold keep their text.",
    "CRASH_RETIRE_BUILT is false until the retire fence is built, so an image cannot mark by configuration without the fence.",
    "A ZDR or waived run never gets a marker and never gets a crash park: the executor's facts exclude it, the worker's retention check refuses it, and the store_proofs Park entry names the tests.",
    "Logs, metrics, events and the tombstone's reason are ids, counts and closed words only (answering, paused, the CrashRefusal labels, the site words); no conversation, tool argument or credential reaches them.",
]

FAILURE_MATRIX = [
    "F1 The executor of an eligible run crashes after a round fold, all switches on, no approval: at the deadline the worker re-seals the fold (seq+1, park, crash_interrupted, due now), the obligation is spared at the crash horizon, RunDetail shows resumable with park_reason crash_interrupted; a park continue claims it, the executor fences, the loop continues, ONE answer is appended and the run completes.",
    "F2 The same crash before any fold exists (round 1): no fold, the committed worker ends the run outcome_unknown at the deadline.",
    "F3 The executor crashes after the retire tombstone, before or after the append: the fold is a tombstone, crash_reseal refuses (NotResumable), the worker terminalizes outcome_unknown as committed (the answer may be on the thread, as committed). Nothing resumes a run that had already answered.",
    "F4 A marked loop pauses for the disclosure-consent read: the tombstone 'paused' is saved before the approval exists; the approval spares the run while pending; when it resolves or expires the run ends as committed (S8-0 on: outcome_unknown), never crash-parked, because the stale boundary fold is gone. If the 'paused' tombstone could not be confirmed, crash_park_run's approvals fact still refuses the run.",
    "F5 An eligible loop A is alive but silent past 15 minutes and is crash-parked. A's session bearer (300 s by default) is dead: its next fold save or retire is Unauthenticated (Denied); with a long-lived bearer it is Stale. A's own last accepted heartbeat is older than 900 s, so the age rule applies: a Denied answer, an unproven writer or any transport failure of the tombstone STOPS the loop; a Stale or Closed answer stops it at any age. A returns Aborted continue_in_progress at its next loop top or at its exit funnel, before any append, receipt or approval; a typed failure (InferFailed, RouteUnavailable) is stopped by the same funnel and writes NO receipt, so the crash park is not terminalized by A's service-token receipt, even when every RPC of the woken loop fails at the transport. A later continue (B) re-infers from the parked fold and answers once.",
    "F6 The same A heartbeats at the right moment: a heartbeat between the worker's claim and its recovery transaction returns the obligation to open, the worker's lease check abandons the pass, the fold stays active, nothing is parked.",
    "F7 A's tombstone save and the worker's re-seal race: the runs row lock orders them. Tombstone first: the worker refuses (not_resumable), terminalizes, A appends after its own save (a run the worker is ending: committed behaviour). Re-seal first: A's save is stale (or its one probe wins the compare-and-set, then A owns the run and a resume's fence is the stale one). Never both an answer and a live crash park.",
    "F8 An approval continuation (segment or in place), a delegated loop, a Space, ZDR, waived, unpinned, client-tool or MCP-tool run, an effect-capable run (plan_mode false or a rung above read_only): never marked; crash_reseal would refuse them anyway; terminalized at the committed deadline.",
    "F9 A marked run crashes with a row in session_tool_audit_intents or in approvals: refused (ledger_not_empty, approval_exists), terminalized as committed.",
    "F10 A deploy or config drift between crash and resume (prompt digest, tool names, research switch, server-resolved view, an image skew between crash_reseal and check_park_fold): the first continue closes the fold (park_not_restorable) and the run ends at the renewed deadline; if nobody continues, the crash TTL ends it (outcome_unknown), SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_TTL_SECONDS (default 3600) after the re-seal, which itself happens at the 15-minute deadline: 75 minutes after the last heartbeat by default.",
    "F11 A continue whose route no longer resolves: park_route_unavailable, no close, no default route (S8-A); the lease lapses; the crash TTL ends it.",
    "F12 The gateway park form, the BFF flag, an image below S8-7 or S8-8, an executor resume switch, or the GATEWAY's own AGENT_CONTINUE_AFTER_APPROVAL_ENABLED or EXECUTION_LOOP_RESUME_ENABLED (the committed S7 rollback turns the gateway off first) is off while crash parks exist: the continue is refused (continue_disabled, not_resumable or a 400); the parks are held for the crash TTL and then end outcome_unknown. The kill order forbids turning them off first.",
    "F13 OLD session-core (below S8-B) with a NEW executor, marking on: folds carry an inert extension key, the tombstone is an ordinary valid fold the store accepts, and no crash park ever exists. The run differs from committed in: one extra RPC at its end, a pre_effect save before plan and delegation rounds, and the ownership stop (a run cancelled or ended under the loop, or a store that refuses it, ends the loop without a late answer or receipt; a duplicate dispatch's loser stops). These are flip (5)'s visible effects, owner-gated.",
    "F14 NEW session-core with crash park on and an OLD executor (below S8-B, or marking off): the folds carry no marker, crash_reseal refuses (NotMarked), every run is terminalized as committed.",
    "F15 SESSION_CORE_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED off, park recovery off or the store off with eligible folds: the committed worker; existing crash parks are still spared (park recovery on) until the CRASH TTL (not the park TTL) and are claimable; with park recovery off each is terminalized within 15 minutes and a continue gets not_resumable.",
    "F16 The descriptor key is missing in the worker (DescriptorCipher::from_env fails): Refused(key_unavailable), terminalized as committed. A fold sealed under another AAD: Refused(did_not_authenticate), terminalized.",
    "F17 Two session-core replicas pick the same overdue run: SKIP LOCKED and the lease let one in; if both reach the fold, the second finds a park (spared) and not an active fold. Replicas of different images (S8-A and S8-B) decide per obligation: an S8-A replica spares a crash park under the park TTL; drain before a rolling deploy.",
    "F18 The worker's transaction fails or session-core restarts mid re-seal: it rolls back, the obligation lease lapses after 60 s, the pass is retried; no partial park exists.",
    "F19 Cancel while crash-parked: cancelled, the fold purged and RUN_CANCELLED in one transaction; the obligation is superseded on the next pass; a later continue is not_resumable. Cancel of a LIVE marked run: the loop's next save or its funnel gets run_ended (Closed) and it stops with no late answer or receipt (committed: it appends after the cancel): visible effect of flip (5).",
    "F20 The crash TTL passes (the deadline plus the TTL after the last heartbeat): one outcome_unknown terminal through the unchanged path, the fold purged, mp_session_managed_parks_expired_total{reason=crash}. A typed park of another run keeps the park TTL.",
    "F21 The resumed loop B crashes after its fence: its fold is a marked boundary fold again (fence fold, seed Parked, payload parks carried); the worker parks it again; at five parks (typed and crash together) the next crash is terminalized.",
    "F22 A crash park is claimed (state resuming) and B dies before its fence: the lease lapses after 120 s and the park can be claimed again; the S8-A spare keeps it until the crash TTL.",
    'F23 The retire save fails Unavailable or times out three times (a healthy loop, last heartbeat under 780 s old): the loop proceeds to the append (fail open). The tombstone may or may not have committed; if it did, the run is safe; if not, the documented residual R3 applies (and it needs a failed receipt or a crash as well). The same three failures with a heartbeat at or past 780 s STOP the loop (a worker may already have parked the run).',
    "F24 The retire save is answered Stale, Closed or run_ended: the loop returns Aborted continue_in_progress at any heartbeat age. Answered Unauthenticated, PermissionDenied or NotFound it stops only at or past the fail-open window (a healthy loop whose bearers just expired proceeds and writes the committed immediate failed receipt). A stop: a fresh run's stream answers agent_dispatch_unavailable plus RUN_DISPATCH_DEGRADED and terminalizes nothing; a park continue stream gets a park_continue continue_in_progress frame through park_dispatch_of and nothing is terminalized.",
    "F25 An UNMARKED loop (switch off, ineligible run) meets a stale save: unchanged, the writer fails and holds effects, the loop goes on and finalizes as committed.",
    "F26 The last allowed round: the boundary fold after it carries no marker (no round left), so a crash then is terminalized; a resume of an earlier park with one round left is marked until that round is spent.",
    "F27 EXECUTION_LOOP_CRASH_PARK_ENABLED is turned off, or execution-core or model-gateway restarts or is deployed, while (5) and (6) are on: a switch is container environment, so flipping it recreates the executor and every in-flight loop dies; a gateway restart drops the RunAgent call and the executor's handler future with it (no funnel, no receipt). Every in-flight marked run is crash-parked at its deadline and, with no resumer, held for the deadline plus the TTL; after an image change the first continue usually fails park_not_restorable. Killing (5) alone while (6) is on therefore crash-parks the in-flight runs, so (6) goes off first whatever order the owner flipped them in.",
    "F28 A crash park exists and the executor image is rolled back below S8-B: it resumes the park (S8-A code), never marks again. Rolled back below S8-A: it cannot resume (resume_incomplete); the parks are held for the crash TTL.",
    "F29 A pinned marked run pauses cold (no pause fold exists for a pinned run) and the 'paused' tombstone is not confirmed (a transient failure after three attempts, fail open): the stored fold is still the marked boundary fold, but crash_park_run refuses a run with any approvals row, so after the approval is consumed, denied or expired the run ends as committed, never crash-parked.",
    "F30 session-core rolled back to an S8-A image while crash parks exist: they are spared for the PARK TTL (24 h), claimable, resumable, and no zombie fence exists beyond the seq compare-and-set; the rollback rule says drain first.",
    "F31 A park at the credential deadline (parking and crash marking both on) is answered park_accepted false (NotAccepted): try_park closes its own row at the seq the store answered (best effort) and the writer becomes Off(SelfClosed); the loop returns the committed OutOfTime reply and writes its receipt as S8-A does. It is NOT read as a lost ownership. If the close does not land, the stray row is a typed park that finalize's terminal transition purges; the one race (replicas disagreeing about park recovery, a claimant fencing the row before the close lands) is S8-A's own exposure.",
    "F31a The same park save is AMBIGUOUS (a timeout or a lost response). A marked loop does NOT close expected+1 and does NOT mark itself closed: the writer stays Active and the funnel's tombstone at the expected seq settles it. The park did not commit: the tombstone succeeds and the loop finalizes (a second answer is impossible without it). The park did commit: the tombstone's one probe overwrites the loop's own park and the loop proceeds. An UNCLAIMED crash park sits at that seq (the loop was superseded but alive, with a valid bearer): the tombstone is Stale and the probe takes the run back, so exactly one loop proceeds. A resume already fenced (N+2): Stale and the loop stops. A dead bearer: Denied and the age rule decides. A park that committed followed by a Denied tombstone and a stop leaves the loop's own typed credential_window park spared for the PARK TTL (24 h), resumable, with no RunParked event (the stream shows RUN_DISPATCH_DEGRADED). An UNMARKED loop closes expected+1 as S8-A does.",
    "F32 A marked loop's executor is paused or partitioned past the deadline, is crash-parked, a user continues (B claims and fences), and the stalled executor wakes: its saves are Denied or Stale, its funnel returns the stop; B is never cut off by a receipt from the old loop.",
    "F33 A live marked loop whose end-of-round save timed out (ambiguous) is crash-parked before its next save: its probe at seq+1 can match the re-sealed seq and take the park back; if a resume had claimed but not fenced, that resume's fence is stale. One loop proceeds.",
    "F34 Version skew: session-core's crash_reseal and execution-core's check_park_fold disagree after a change to one of them: crash parks are created and every first continue closes them (park_not_restorable); held for the crash TTL. The oracle test in S8B-2 guards one tree; the deploy order and the drain-before-rollback rule guard two.",
    "F35 A marked loop's plan.propose or subagent.* round: the open-round pre_effect fold is saved first (only while the writer is Active). A save answered Stale, Closed or Denied (ownership lost) holds the call; a transient failure, or a writer that failed or is off for another reason, does NOT hold it (the call is dispatched as committed code dispatches it; a crash then parks the boundary before the call and a resume repeats it). After a successful fence a crash inside the round leaves an unmarked fold (OpenRound), so the run is terminalized as committed; after the round's end-of-round fold the loop is marked again.",
    "F37 The SPA follows a crash-parked run: runs.status stays running for the deadline plus the crash TTL, no run_parked frame arrives, the composer is held in its streaming state on every thread open for up to the SPA's fixed 15 minutes (a typed message is held), then 'unknown'; the only exit is Stop, which cancels the run and purges the park. Listed, not fixed here (no SPA change in S8-B).",
    "F38 A marked loop's writer failed definitively for a non-ownership reason (Refused(KeyUnavailable | Unimplemented)) or is Off (loop_checkpoint_disabled): the funnel makes no RPC and proceeds at once (no sleep), finalize runs as committed; the visible calls are dispatched. If another replica holds the key and crash-parks the marked fold stored earlier, a superseded loop could still end the run: the drain-before-rolling rule and R19b.",
    'F39 A marked loop whose bearers expire mid-run: with a recent last heartbeat (under 780 s) its funnel or end-of-round save answers Denied and the loop keeps the committed behaviour, an immediate failed receipt; a delegation or plan round that overruns has an unmarked stored fold, so it is never crash-parked in any case. A resume B whose bearer overran mid-round and is silent past the window stops, and its park-continue stream gets a park_continue continue_in_progress frame; 15 minutes later the run is parked again with parks+1 (the deadline again), repeatable up to the cap of 5.',
    'F40 An UNARMED root loop (the S8B image with the switch off, or an ineligible run) reaches a loop-owned pause or a failed writer at the pause site: retire_fence returns Ok at once (its first statement is the armed check) and the approval is raised exactly as in S8-A, even when the writer already failed Stale.',
    "F41 A degraded session-core while (5) is on: a plan or delegation round waits up to the 10 s gated timeout plus one probe before dispatch; a run end waits up to about 6.4 s for three tombstone attempts; the committed finalize failure follows. Listed with flip (5)'s effects.",
    'F42 With (6) on and the worker missing its descriptor key: every recovered run with an active fold counts mp_session_loop_crash_park_unreadable_total{key_unavailable} (the operational family, not the refused family) and is terminalized as committed; an owner alert belongs on the unreadable family.',
    "F36 A new user turn is appended to a thread while its run is crash-parked: the resume's answer lands after it (inherited S8-A behaviour).",
]

AMENDMENTS = [
    "AGAINST v4 (the crash-park half of s8-v4.json), each with the review finding it answers:\n- THE THREAD WATERMARK and migration 0049 are DROPPED (findings 3 of rounds 1 and 2: the clock claim; round 3 critical: the claim re-check): the answer is fenced by a tombstone ordered through the fold's own seq, so nothing compares messages with the fold and nothing locks the threads row.\n- loop_checkpoint_superseded, the segment comparison in save, SaveError's flag and the `loop_superseded` token are DROPPED: the executor stops on a definitive Stale, Closed, Denied or NotFound, which the store already says, and reports with the existing closed token continue_in_progress (a new token would have needed the gateway lists, the SPA tuple, the BFF parity test and four guards for a distinction a marked loop does not need).\n- fence_answer as a save of the live conversation is REPLACED by retire (a tombstone: no conversation retained, and exactly 'do not resume from here'), widened to every exit that reaches finalize (typed failures included, a gap the first draft of this design had) and to the second act nobody can take back, raising an approval.\n- THE CRASH GRACE (900 s) and the heartbeat push are DROPPED: for read-only runs with a fenced exit they bought only latency. The re-seal is due at once.\n- CrashFacts' ledger_after_fold with its timestamp and the release-owner check are REPLACED by two facts that use no clock: the run has no ledger row at all and no approvals row at all.\n- park_crashed's list of facts is REPLACED by the pure crash_reseal shared with the executor's oracle test (round 3 critical: the marker must mean park-resumable at rest).\n- EXT_PARKABLE is now computed from the allowlist the loop really runs under as well as from the request kind (round 3 suggested fix), requires a read-only run (new), and carries the identifiers in ONE payload key instead of spreading the S8-A park keys over every fold.\n- The third writer_gate and the park-aware claim re-check are NOT needed and are not built.\n- v4's statement that effect-capable runs are crash-parkable is REVERSED: v1 covers read-only runs only.",
    "AGAINST S8-A AS BUILT (what S8B-1..S8B-4 change in committed S8-A code and tests):\n- terminalization.rs PARK_SPARE_HORIZON_SQL gains a fourth bind and the CASE on park_reason for the wait in both places; spare_parked_run gains a third argument; PARK_HELD_SQL becomes PARK_HELD_REASON_SQL. The guards park_spare_violations and the_park_spare_follows_the_approval_spare_and_precedes_the_terminal_write pin exact strings (`WHERE run_id = $1 AND kind = 'park' AND state IN ('parked','resuming')\\n        AND updated_at`, `spare_parked_run(`, `if park_recovery_active() {`): S8B-1 amends them and their mutation rows in the SAME commit (the two `$2` horizon needles, the exact-string row that removes `AND updated_at + make_interval(secs => $2) > now()` and its assert_ne!, the `spare_parked_run(` and `if park_recovery_active() {` rows), and adds the crash branch to the order they pin (after the spare, before the held-reason read and the terminal write).\n- durable_loop_contract park_writer_violations, run_parkable, StaticFacts (text) and park_fold are NOT changed: the marker is one new key and run_crash_parkable is an independent function, so the park-key rule, the run_parkable needles and every mutation row of the_park_writer_guard_goes_red_when_the_code_it_guards_regresses stay as committed. What changes: the StaticFacts literal in run_rounds is hoisted into a local (the builder re-verifies the guards that read it and amends only text that moved), try_park gains one note_self_closed statement (NotAccepted arm) and a conditional on its ambiguous arm's close (`!folds.is_fenced()`; the try_park rules about close_stray_park( appearing at least twice, park_fold and NotAccepted are re-verified), and OffReason gains a variant (its exhaustive match gains an arm; tests that list the reasons gain the new one).\n- fold.rs Snapshot gains one field: every Snapshot literal in agent.rs (5 production sites and one test literal), park.rs's test and fold.rs's tests change (compile-driven); park_at_boundary passes None so park folds are unchanged.\n- store_proofs(): the Park entry gains the S8B tests that drive the zero-retention and waived gate; switch_table(): two rows. every_guard_goes_red_when_the_code_it_guards_regresses keeps every committed row unchanged; the_park_writer_guard_goes_red_when_the_code_it_guards_regresses loses exactly three row ANCHORS to the async block's re-indent (the Site B ParkPoint row and two rows that passed by substring luck), re-anchored whitespace-insensitively in S8B-3.\n- S8-A's ledger text and failure-matrix row 19 ('the executor crashes during a park resume after the fence: ... no crash-park') are superseded when S8-B is on: that run is crash-parked again, up to the cap. S8-A's invariants 3 ('the executor never writes crash_interrupted') and 10 (the TTL) hold; invariant 10 gains 'a crash park uses the crash TTL'.\n- RunDetail.park_reason can now be crash_interrupted; the SPA never reads it (run-park.ts reads the run_parked frame, which only the executor's typed parks produce) and its comment 'reserved for a later slice' becomes stale (optional comment-only change in S8B-5).",
    "AGAINST THE FIVE NAMED DEFECTS, where each lives: (1) approach 3(1), crash_reseal, run_crash_parkable, tool_names_derivable, the visible-call fence, the oracle test, the crash TTL; (2) approach 2, retire_fence, the exit funnel, lost_ownership, the ordering DB test; (3) approach 3(3), the crash_park_run source scan; (4) approach 3(4) and F13/F14; (5) approach 6 and the steps' KILL ORDER and ROLLBACK paragraphs.",
    "CLAIMS IN EARLIER TEXT THAT S8-B CORRECTS: (a) the S8 v3 and v4 designs said the worker's EXISTS on messages serializes with append_message_in_tx; it does not (append locks threads, the worker locked runs), and S8-B does not rely on it; (b) v3 named a relation tool_action_effect_ledger; it does not exist (session_tool_audit_intents does), and S8-B names the real one and uses it only as 'any row'; (c) 'a delegated subagent may never run an effectful tool' is true only of the risky list: a child can run a Write-class call (for example save_memory) that is not on it, with no fold fence and a ledger row, which is why S8-B v1 requires the read_only rung (whose gate covers every depth) rather than relying on the leaf blocklist; (d) a first draft of this design and the v4 design said a zombie is stopped by a stale fold save: a loop silent past 900 s holds session bearers that expired at 300 s, so its saves are Denied before any seq is compared, and its terminal receipt and heartbeat use fresh service tokens; S8-B treats Denied as lost ownership and fences the receipt; (e) the committed heartbeat and finalize let a loop end a run that was cancelled under it: S8-B stops a MARKED loop in that case (flip (5)'s visible effect) and leaves every unmarked loop as committed.",
]

OPEN_QUESTIONS = [
    "OWNER (open): WHEN MAY CRASH-PARK BE FLIPPED? Not decided here. Proposed prerequisites for the owner to accept or change: (i) the S8-A flips (1) to (3) are on and the S8-A park resume has passed its live stage s8a-C; (ii) something calls the resume route (a UI button or an automatic resume): without it crash-park only delays outcome_unknown from ~15 minutes to the crash TTL; (iii) the crash TTL is chosen; (iv) flip (5) is itself a decision, not an observation: its visible effects are listed in the risks (R4) and the steps; the per-run armed info! line is the evidence, execution-core records no metrics; its ORDER against (6) is also the owner's ((5) then (6) is the proposal; (6) first is dormant and defers (5)'s effects); (iv-b) the SPA does not recognise a crash park (R19a): the composer is held on every thread open and Stop cancels the run and purges the park; a gateway/BFF projection of resumable and park_reason plus an SPA 'interrupted' tail with a non-cancelling dismiss may be set as a prerequisite of (6); (v) the S8B-6 live proof has passed. Flip (6) last, owner-gated.",
    "OWNER (open): WHETHER A PARK SHOULD GIVE THE THREAD A NOTICE. Not decided and not designed. Facts for the decision: an executor park (typed stop) appends nothing today (the committed failure path appended an explanation, a park does not); a crash park has no executor stream and no gateway involvement, so a notice would have to be appended by session-core's worker through the same append path (and must not count as a message after the fold, which is irrelevant here because crash-park reads no messages); a notice must be fixed, content-free text and must not reach a ZDR or waived run (they never park); ordering relative to the eventual answer and a duplicate notice on a second park are product questions.",
    "OWNER (open): THE CRASH TTL. Default 3600 s with a clamp of 60 s to 30 days is a proposal. It is the longest a crash park nothing resumes can delay outcome_unknown BEYOND the 15-minute deadline, which the re-seal itself waits for: the total is 15 minutes plus the TTL (75 minutes by default; no value gives the committed 15). Alternatives: the park TTL (24 h, simpler, costs a day), or a few minutes if a resumer will act at once.",
    "OWNER (open): EXTEND TO EFFECT-CAPABLE RUNS? v1 refuses them because a crash makes their effects unknowable and the fold fence covers only root effects (a child can run a Write-class call with no fold save). Extending needs: the v4 ledger-after-fold fact (reserved_at against the fold's updated_at, both database now(), with a skew margin that makes it conservative) plus a fence that stops a zombie's later reservations (a loop identity on ReserveToolAction, or a store check against a crash-parked fold), plus a policy on a possibly-effected call. Recommended only after a resumer exists.",
    "OWNER (open): EXTEND TO RUNS THAT SEND CLIENT TOOLS? The gateway's park form sends no tools, so a resume cannot offer them; marking such runs would hold them for the TTL. Needs either the client tools stored in the fold (a content decision) or the resume re-supplied with them (a gateway contract change). Note the SPA's subscription Do turn sends none, so this concerns other callers.",
    "OWNER (open): ACCEPT THE RESIDUAL DUPLICATE ANSWER (R3), or fund the exact belt? The belt is a nullable thread-message watermark on run_loop_checkpoints stamped inside every fold save from the messages table's identity sequence (never from a clock), plus a claim that takes the thread row lock before it re-checks. It needs migration 0049 and was the last open clock argument of v4.",
    "OWNER (open): ACCEPT THE VISIBLE EFFECTS OF FLIP (5) (R4): no late answer or receipt from a marked loop whose run was cancelled or ended under it, none from a live loop silent past the deadline when bearers are long-lived, recovery instead of an immediate failed receipt for a marked loop that overran its credentials?",
    "OWNER/LEAD (open): THE COVERAGE COST OF THE VISIBLE-CALL FENCE (R13). A crash inside a plan-proposing or delegation round is not parkable (after a successful fence). The alternative is to drop the fence and accept a second plan proposal or a second delegation record after a resume.",
    'OWNER/LEAD (open): THE AUTOMATIC RESUMER, if the owner chooses one as the prerequisite: it needs backoff and a per-run crash budget below the park cap (R19c) or a poison run can kill an executor five times and every in-flight run with it.',
    "Integrator: nothing to record in plan 4.3 (no wire change). Record the three S8-B settings (two switches and the TTL) in the switch table of the ledger entry.",
    "Lead: while reading the heartbeat I found (not touched, not in scope): heartbeat_managed_agent_run ignores already_terminal for EVERY run, so a cancelled run's live loop is not stopped by it. S8-B stops a MARKED loop through the fence only. A separate small item for the unmarked loops.",
    "Lead (optional follow-ups, none needed for S8-B): (H1) a background liveness beat in the executor so that 15 minutes of silence means a dead loop (changes the heartbeat contract of every run; needs a hung-loop bound); (H2) an initial fold before round 1 so a crash in the first round is also parkable; (H3) reject a heartbeat while the fold is a crash park in state parked, and a store-side refusal of an ExecutionAgent receipt while the fold is a crash park (stop a zombie one round earlier; defense in depth; the funnel already covers the receipt).",
    "Builder: the oracle test lives in execution-core (it can call mp-contracts and park.rs both); keep it in S8B-2's test list so S8B-2 cannot merge without it, and do not weaken crash_reseal to make it pass. Hoisting the StaticFacts literal and adding two statements to try_park are the only edits to S8-A code outside tests and SQL; re-run park_writer_violations and its guard test after each.",
]

